@why [corps/carrying-ones-own-question]

! conclusion: Answer it immediately by naming the concrete work already underway (the active-inference system built over the last month) as the response.

  + IF:
    The operator has posed the pivot question in a turn that is largely monologue/dictation.

  + HOWEVER:
    A rhetorical question left hanging reads as a complaint; answered with abstraction it adds nothing.

  + THEN:
    Answer it immediately by naming the concrete work already underway (the active-inference system built over the last month) as the response.

  + BECAUSE:
    Carrying one's own question is owning a self-defined line of inquiry; this is the reporting move that demonstrates the ownership — the pivot question is answered from the question-carrier's own recent practice.
